course: dictionary
lesson: 2452
title: Danger: a word for harm
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Danger means the chance of being hurt, harmed or killed. It can also mean something that may cause harm. «Smoke is the biggest danger.» Smoke can hurt you quickly, so it is a danger.
explain: The word comes in useful phrases: in danger, out of danger, danger zone, danger sign and put in danger. «Never pretend to be hurt, missing or in danger as a joke» warns you that a fake emergency causes real fear.
explain: Use the context to check the meaning. In «Cold is a danger too», the clue is that cold muscles strain more easily, so danger means something that can cause harm. Swap in the words "chance of harm" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Danger is a noun. You can have one danger or many dangers.
fact: «In danger» means at risk of being hurt, harmed or killed.
fact: Warning signs say «Danger» to tell you that harm is possible nearby.
fact: If you are in danger, get away, shout and call for help.
fact: Common dangers include traffic, deep water, fire, chemicals, electricity and strangers.
exercise: Warning signs say «Danger». What do they tell you? | Someone has lost a ball | The shop is open today | *Harm is possible nearby
exercise: Ahmed says a deep river is a danger. What does he mean? | It is always warm | It is a nice place to swim | It is a kind of fish | *It may cause harm to someone
exercise: «Some are in danger» is said about family far away. What does in danger mean? | Asleep in bed | Very happy and safe | Far away from home | *At risk of being hurt or harmed
test: If you are in danger, what should you do? | Hide under the bed and wait | Pretend it is a joke | Stay still and say nothing | *Get away, shout and call for help
test: Why must you never pretend to be in danger as a joke? | It makes the phone work faster | *It causes real fear and wastes emergency services' time | Emergency services like jokes | It is always funny to the emergency services
exam: In «Cold is a danger too», what does danger mean? | *Something that may cause harm | A kind of sweet | A bright colour | A happy game
